   "source": [
    "# 1. INTRODUCTION\n",
    "India's retail payments landscape has shifted rapidly since 2022, moving away from cash-based ATM and POS usage toward card- and QR-based digital payments. The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) publishes monthly, bank-wise statistics covering ATM/CRM infrastructure, POS and QR (Bharat QR / UPI QR) infrastructure, credit- and debit-card issuance, and the volume and value of card-based transactions across payment channels (POS, online and other) and cash withdrawals.\n",
    "This report documents a complete data analytics workflow data cleaning, feature engineering, exploratory data analysis, and interpretation performed on the RBI bank-wise dataset for the period March 2022 to September 2025, to understand how physical banking infrastructure, digital payment infrastructure, and card-based transaction activity have evolved across five categories of Indian banks: Public Sector, Private Sector, Foreign, Small Finance and Payment Banks.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "eb1a1795-cf82-4aef-a551-c234a52f7d2b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 1.1 Project scope\n",
    "\n",
    "The scope of this project was to analyse monthly bank-level payment data across different categories of Indian banks."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "dd13df0f-7ffc-4233-91aa-50f853c467f2",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 2. OBJECTIVES\n",
    "1.Clean and prepare the raw RBI data into an analysis-ready, consistent dataset.\n",
    "\n",
    "2.Engineer summary indicators (total infrastructure, total cards, total transaction volume/value) that answer business questions more directly than the raw, channel-level columns.\n",
    "\n",
    "3.Explore the distribution, trends and relationships in the data using univariate, bivariate, multivariate, time-series, category-level and bank-level analysis.\n",
    "\n",
    "4.Identify significant patterns, correlations and anomalies in banking infrastructure and digital payment adoption.\n",
    "\n",
    "5.Summarize the findings into actionable insights and recommendations on India's shift from cash to digital payments.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6d141dcd-442e-4366-9cc1-d49d317589cb",
   "metadata": {
    "jp-MarkdownHeadingCollapsed": true
   },
   "source": [
    "# 3. DATASET DESCRIPTION\n",
    "The raw file contains 2,671 monthly bank-level records across 30 columns, covering 67 unique banks grouped into 5 bank categories (Public Sector,Private Sector, Foreign, Small Finance and Payment Banks), over 43 months from March 2022 to September 2025. Each row represents one bank's activity in one calendar month — the dataset is structured as a bank × month panel, which is why grouping by bank_name, bank_category and date/year is used throughout the analysis to answer different questions.\n",
    "Section 5.3 of this report (Feature Engineering) adds derived \"total\" columns on top of this raw structure (e.g. total_cards, total_atms_crms, total_cc_payment_value) so that later analysis can work with whole-portfolio figures instead of repeatedly summing channel-level columns. After cleaning and feature engineering, the analysis-ready dataset expands to 42 columns while retaining all 2,671 records.\n",
    "### Dataset Column Groups\n",
    "| Group | Example Columns | What It Measures |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| Identifiers | id, date, bank_category, bank_name | Which bank, category, and month a row belongs to |\n",
    "| Physical Infrastructure | atms_crms_onsite, atms_crms_offsite, pos, micro_atms | Number of ATM/CRM and POS/micro-ATM terminals deployed |\n",
    "| Digital QR Infrastructure | bharat_qr, upi_qr | Number of QR-code payment access points deployed |\n",
    "| Card Base | credit_cards, debit_cards | Number of cards issued and outstanding |\n",
    "| Credit-Card Transactions | cc_pay_trns_*_vol, cc_pay_trns_*_val, cc_cash_withdraw_atm_* | Volume and value of credit-card payments and ATM cash withdrawals |\n",
    "| Debit-Card Transactions | dc_pay_trns_*_vol, dc_pay_trns_*_val, dc_cash_withdraw_* | Volume and value of debit-card payments and cash withdrawals through ATM and POS |\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
