   "source": [
    "# 4.3 Data Cleaning\n",
    "\n",
    "The raw data is cleaned so that later aggregations and charts are not distorted by duplicate entities, missing values, or incorrect data types. Cleaning follows a fixed order: (1) standardize categorical labels, (2) treat missing values based on why they are missing rather than a single default rule, (3) correct data types, (4) detect  but not blindly remove  outliers, and (5) run sanity checks. This order matters: for example, fixing bank names before grouping avoids creating a false duplicate bank, and filling missing values before casting to int64 avoids a type-conversion error, since integers cannot hold missing values.\n",
    "\n",
    "| Issue found | Treatment applied | Why |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| \"Catholic Syrian Bank\" and \"CSB Bank\" are the same institution | Standardized to \"CSB Bank\" via an explicit `.replace()` mapping | Prevents the same bank from being split into two entities during grouping/aggregation |\n",
    "| Missing `atms_crms_onsite` / `atms_crms_offsite` (23 rows) | Filled with 0 | Absence of reported infrastructure is a structural zero, not an unknown value |\n",
    "| Missing `cc_` columns for India Post Payments Bank, Mar–Apr 2022 (2 rows) | Filled with 0 | Payments Banks are not RBI-licensed to issue credit cards, so these are structural zeros |\n",
    "| `cc_` / `atms_` columns upcast to `float64` | Cast back to `int64` after nulls were filled | These are physical counts and transaction volumes, which should not display as decimals |\n",
    "| Potential outliers in every numeric column (IQR test) | Retained, not removed | Outliers most likely reflect genuine differences in bank operating scale rather than data errors |\n",
    "| Duplicate rows / bank-category mismatches / whitespace | Verified as zero via sanity checks | Confirms the cleaned data is safe to aggregate without hidden duplication |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4bd66490-dcec-4cde-af64-123b94abf44a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 4.3.1  Standardize Bank Names\n",
    "Inconsistent naming of the same bank can create duplicate entities during grouping and aggregation.During data inspection, `Catholic Syrian Bank` and`CSB Bank` were identified as two names referring to the same institution.Therefore, `Catholic Syrian Bank` is standardized to `CSB Bank`.\n",
    "This ensures that all monthly observations belonging to the same bank are treated as a single entity during subsequent analysis."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 11,
   "id": "01d3d69f-5f51-46d2-8a25-d0ab032986d3",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df[\"bank_name\"] = df[\"bank_name\"].replace(\n",
    "    {\"Catholic Syrian Bank\": \"CSB Bank\"})"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f161d902-05d7-4380-b7dc-f15324b0145d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 4.3.2 Handle Missing Values"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e4e1e4b4-9906-425c-9e20-36480db57b14",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 4.3.2.1 ATMS_CRMS_ONSITE and ATMS_CRMS_OFFSITE\n",
    "The columns `atms_crms_onsite` and `atms_crms_offsite` contain a small number of missing values.Based on the structure of the dataset, these missing values occur for banks where the corresponding ATM/CRM infrastructure was not reported or was not applicable for that observation.Since the variable represents the number of physical ATM/CRM units, the absence of reported infrastructure is treated as zero.Therefore, missing values in these columns are replaced with `0`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 12,
   "id": "6f8ec4b0-a626-4fb9-9dc5-b1b922d77ddd",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "atm_cols = [\"atms_crms_onsite\", \"atms_crms_offsite\"]\n",
    "df[atm_cols] = df[atm_cols].fillna(0)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e77f54af-1a52-45d0-8a06-330e7f843777",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 4.3.2.2 Credit Card columns for India Post Payments Bank (Mar & Apr 2022)\n",
    "Missing values were also identified in the credit-card transaction variables.Payments Banks are not RBI-licensed to issue credit cards, the missing values represent structural zeros rather than missing measurements.Therefore, these missing values are replaced with `0`.This treatment is appropriate because replacing these observations with statistical estimates such as the mean or median would incorrectly imply that credit-card activity existed for those bank-month observations."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 13,
   "id": "55603f1e-5c5d-4a43-b62d-801cdd67afe9",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "cc_cols = [c for c in df.columns if c.startswith(\"cc_\")]\n",
    "df[cc_cols] = df[cc_cols].fillna(0)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 14,
   "id": "36e47d97-4aa5-4031-acae-3882898f8ce2",
   "metadata": {},
