   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 4.3.3 Correct Data Types\n",
    "Several cc_/atms_ columns were upcast to float64 because of the NaN values. Now that nulls are filled, cast counts back to integer types for consistency with their dc_ counterparts. Missing values can cause numerical count variables to be automatically stored as `float64`.After missing values have been handled, count-based variables are converted back to integer data types.\n",
    "The following variables are treated as integer-like measures:\n",
    "- ATM/CRM counts\n",
    "- Credit-card transaction volumes\n",
    "- Credit-card ATM withdrawal volumes\n",
    "Correct data types improve consistency, memory efficiency and interpretation of the dataset."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 15,
   "id": "a850e9aa-1fe6-4ff6-8f3a-486be2296d39",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "int_like_cols = [\n",
    "    \"atms_crms_onsite\", \"atms_crms_offsite\",\n",
    "    \"cc_pay_trns_at_pos_vol\", \"cc_pay_trns_online_vol\", \"cc_pay_trns_other_vol\",\n",
    "    \"cc_cash_withdraw_atm_vol\",\n",
    "]\n",
    "for c in int_like_cols:\n",
    "    df[c] = df[c].astype(\"int64\")"
