    "# 4.3.4 Detect Outliers - IQR Outlier Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "The Interquartile Range (IQR) method is used to identify potential outliers in the numerical variables of the dataset. Q1 and Q3 are calculated for \n",
    "each variable, and the IQR is calculated as the difference between Q3 and Q1. The lower and upper limits are determined using 1.5 times the IQR. Values \n",
    "outside these limits are considered potential outliers.\n",
    "\n",
    "Key findings:-\n",
    "\n",
    "The IQR and box plot analysis identified potential outliers in several numerical variables. These extreme observations indicate variation in \n",
    "banking infrastructure, card usage and transaction activity across the dataset. The outliers were retained because they may represent genuine differences in the operational scale of banks rather than data errors.\n",
    "\n",
    "Recommendation:-\n",
    "\n",
    "The identified outliers should be retained and used for bank segmentation and benchmarking, as they may represent genuine differences in bank size and transaction volumes rather than data errors."
