    "# 7. EXPLORATORY DATA ANALYSIS (EDA)\n",
    "\n",
    "Exploratory Data Analysis is performed to understand the patterns, distributions, relationships and trends present in the cleaned dataset. The analysis uses both statistical methods and visualizations to explore banking infrastructure, card adoption, digital payment infrastructure and transaction activity.\n",
    "\n",
    "The EDA is organized into eight categories :\n",
    "1. Univariate Analysis\n",
    "2. Bivariate Analysis\n",
    "3. Multivariate Analysis\n",
    "4. Time-Series Analysis\n",
    "5. Category-Level Analysis\n",
    "6. Bank-Level Ranking Analysis\n",
    "7. Correlation Analysis\n",
    "8. Composition Analysis,\n",
    "\n",
    "because each answers a different kind of question: univariate analysis describes a single variable's shape; bivariate/multivariate analysis look at relationships between variables; time-series analysis looks at change over the study period; category- and bank-level analysis identify who is driving the numbers; correlation analysis quantifies relationships across many variables at once; and composition analysis breaks a total into its channel-level parts. The table below summarizes every chart used in this project and the reasoning behind the chart-type choice, followed by a chart-by-chart discussion with the actual figures produced."
