    "## Analysis and Visualization Strategy\n",
    "\n",
    "| **Analysis** | **Chart Type** | **Why this chart was chosen** |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| Credit card distribution | Histogram + KDE | Shows how frequently value ranges occur, revealing concentration, spread and skewness that summary statistics alone cannot show. |\n",
    "| ATM/CRM infrastructure by category | Vertical bar | Compares one summed quantity across a small number of discrete groups; bar length is the clearest way to compare magnitude. |\n",
    "| Digital payment infrastructure by category | Multi-series bar | Compares four related infrastructure variables side-by-side per category in a single view. |\n",
    "| Card adoption by category | Grouped bar | Lets credit- and debit-card totals be compared directly within each category. |\n",
    "| Yearly card trend | Line | Year is an ordered axis; a line makes the direction and rate of change over time immediately visible. |\n",
    "| Monthly UPI QR trend | Line | Tracks one metric continuously at fine monthly granularity to read the pace of growth. |\n",
    "| Top 10 banks (cards / UPI QR) | Horizontal bar | Long bank-name labels read better horizontally, and horizontal bars naturally represent a ranking. |\n",
    "| Transaction channel composition (credit/debit) | Pie | Shows how a total (100% of transaction volume) splits into a small number of mutually exclusive parts. |\n",
    "| Credit vs debit transaction value | Bar (2 categories) | Provides a direct magnitude comparison between exactly two totals. |\n",
    "| Cards vs credit-card transaction value | Scatter (with hue) | Reveals the relationship between two continuous variables; colour-by-category adds a third dimension without requiring additional charts. |\n",
    "| Credit cards by category (spread) | Box plot | Shows the full distribution, including median, spread and outliers, rather than only a single average. This is useful when the data is skewed. |\n",
    "| Correlation across 14 indicators | Heatmap | Allows many pairwise relationships to be scanned simultaneously using colour, with exact correlation coefficients annotated. |\n",
    "| Cards & transaction value over time | Dual-axis combo (bar + line) | Combines two metrics on very different scales, such as a count and a monetary value, on one shared time axis. |\n",
    "| All numeric variables (outlier check) | Box plot | Directly visualizes the quartile logic (Q1, median, Q3 and whiskers) used by the numerical IQR outlier test. |"
