    "\n",
    "This analysis of RBI bank-wise ATM/POS/card statistics (2,671 bank-month records, 67 banks, March 2022–September 2025) confirms a clear, ongoing shift in India's retail payments landscape from cash-based to card- and QR-based digital payments. Physical infrastructure remains concentrated in large, traditional Public Sector Banks, while digital (UPI QR) infrastructure is even more concentrated within Private Sector Banks — and within one bank in particular. Credit-card adoption and transaction value are still growing at a healthy pace, while debit-card holdings appear to be approaching saturation. The strong correlations among related indicators confirm the underlying data and derived features are internally consistent, while the moderate correlation between card count and transaction value shows growth is increasingly driven by usage, not just issuance."
